# Nuxt 3 dashboard conventions

This rule applies to:
- `apps/dashboard/` — Pro/Team dashboard (Nuxt app)
- `apps/www/` — marketing site and docs portal
- `packages/nuxt/` — `@agent-firewall/nuxt` integration module for third-party apps

The dashboard and the Nuxt module are separate artifacts. The module is a
reusable library; the dashboard is the hosted product UI. Both are Phase 1.

## Stack reminder

- Nuxt 3 (latest stable)
- Vue 3 with Composition API (NEVER Options API in new code)
- TypeScript strict mode
- Nuxt UI for components
- Tailwind via Nuxt UI
- Pinia for state (only when truly needed — Nuxt's `useState` is often enough)
- Zod for validation (shared with core packages)
- Auth (Pro): nuxt-auth-utils (sessions) or Sidebase nuxt-auth (OAuth)
- Auth (Team/Enterprise): WorkOS SSO — Phase 2

## File organization (Nuxt conventions)

```
apps/dashboard/
├── app.vue                       # Root layout
├── nuxt.config.ts                # Configuration
├── pages/                        # File-based routing
│   ├── index.vue
│   ├── incidents/
│   │   ├── index.vue
│   │   └── [id].vue
│   └── policies/
├── components/                   # Auto-imported
│   ├── IncidentCard.vue
│   └── PolicyEditor.vue
├── composables/                  # Auto-imported (use* prefix)
│   ├── useFirewall.ts
│   └── useAuditLog.ts
├── server/
│   ├── api/                      # API routes (Nitro)
│   │   ├── incidents.get.ts
│   │   └── policies/[id].patch.ts
│   ├── middleware/
│   └── utils/
├── stores/                       # Pinia stores
│   └── workspace.ts
├── utils/                        # Auto-imported helpers
└── types/

packages/nuxt/                    # @agent-firewall/nuxt — integration module
├── src/
│   ├── module.ts                 # defineNuxtModule entry point
│   └── runtime/
│       └── plugins/              # Auto-wrap tools via Nuxt plugin
└── package.json
```

## Component patterns

### Use `<script setup>` always

````vue
<script setup lang="ts">
// ✅ Composition API with <script setup>
import type { AuditEntry } from '@agent-firewall/core';

const props = defineProps<{
  entry: AuditEntry;
}>();

const emit = defineEmits<{
  approve: [id: string];
  deny: [id: string];
}>();
</script>
````

### Component naming

- PascalCase file names: `IncidentCard.vue`, `PolicyEditor.vue`
- Prefix Nuxt UI components with `U`: `UButton`, `UCard`, `UModal`
- Prefix AAF-specific components: `AAFIncidentCard`, `AAFPolicyEditor`

### Props with types, not runtime declarations

````ts
// ❌ Avoid
const props = defineProps({
  entry: { type: Object, required: true }
});

// ✅ Prefer
const props = defineProps<{
  entry: AuditEntry;
  showSignature?: boolean;
}>();
````

## Composables

- Always prefix with `use`: `useFirewall`, `useAuditLog`, `useApprovalQueue`.
- Return refs and computed, not raw values.
- Composables should be pure: no side effects on import.

````ts
// composables/useAuditLog.ts
export function useAuditLog(workspaceId: string) {
  const entries = ref<AuditEntry[]>([]);
  const isLoading = ref(false);

  const verifiedCount = computed(() =>
    entries.value.filter(e => e.verified).length
  );

  async function load() {
    isLoading.value = true;
    entries.value = await $fetch(`/api/workspaces/${workspaceId}/audit`);
    isLoading.value = false;
  }

  return { entries, isLoading, verifiedCount, load };
}
````

## Server routes (Nitro)

- File-based routing in `server/api/`.
- HTTP method as suffix: `incidents.get.ts`, `policies.post.ts`.
- Use `defineEventHandler` always.
- Validate inputs with Zod schemas imported from `@agent-firewall/core`.

````ts
// server/api/incidents/[id]/approve.post.ts
import { z } from 'zod';

const ApproveSchema = z.object({
  approver_id: z.string(),
  reason: z.string().optional(),
});

export default defineEventHandler(async (event) => {
  const id = getRouterParam(event, 'id');
  const body = await readValidatedBody(event, ApproveSchema.parse);

  // Business logic here
  return { ok: true };
});
````

## State management

- Use `useState` from Nuxt for simple shared state across components.
- Use Pinia only for complex state with actions, getters, and persistence.
- NEVER use Vuex (deprecated).

````ts
// ✅ Simple shared state
const currentWorkspace = useState<Workspace | null>('workspace', () => null);

// ✅ Complex state with Pinia
export const useIncidentsStore = defineStore('incidents', () => {
  const list = ref<Incident[]>([]);
  const filters = reactive({ severity: 'all', status: 'open' });

  const filtered = computed(() => /* ... */);

  return { list, filters, filtered };
});
````

## Type sharing with core

The dashboard consumes types from `@agent-firewall/core`. Always import,
never redefine.

````ts
// ❌ Avoid
interface AuditEntry { /* duplicated */ }

// ✅ Prefer
import type { AuditEntry, Decision } from '@agent-firewall/core';
````

## Error handling

- Use `createError` from h3 for API errors.
- Wrap async composables with proper error states.
- Never silently swallow errors.

````ts
// server/api/policies/[id].get.ts
export default defineEventHandler(async (event) => {
  const id = getRouterParam(event, 'id');
  const policy = await db.policy.findUnique({ where: { id } });

  if (!policy) {
    throw createError({
      statusCode: 404,
      statusMessage: 'Policy not found',
    });
  }

  return policy;
});
````

## Performance

- Use `<NuxtLink>` for internal navigation (preloading is automatic).
- Use `<NuxtImg>` for images (automatic optimization).
- Lazy-load heavy components: `const HeavyChart = defineAsyncComponent(...)`.
- Cache server responses where appropriate: `defineCachedEventHandler`.

## SEO and meta

- Use `useSeoMeta` for page-level meta tags.
- Use `useHead` for more granular control.
- Marketing pages (`apps/www/`) must have proper meta tags.

````vue
<script setup>
useSeoMeta({
  title: 'Incidents — Agent Action Firewall',
  description: 'Review and manage agent incidents in real time.',
});
</script>
````

## What NOT to do in Nuxt code

❌ Do NOT use Options API for new components. Composition API only.
❌ Do NOT use Vuex. Use Pinia or `useState`.
❌ Do NOT use `defineComponent`. Use `<script setup lang="ts">`.
❌ Do NOT bypass `$fetch` with raw `fetch`. `$fetch` handles auth, errors, SSR.
❌ Do NOT put business logic in components. Extract to composables.
❌ Do NOT import from `vue` directly when Nuxt auto-imports work
   (`ref`, `computed`, `watch` are auto-imported).
